  "question": {
    "text": "At the centre of a current-carrying circular coil of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, magnetic field due to earth is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The current flowing through the coil, so that it equals the Earth's magnetic field, is"
